    {
      "reader": "reader-a",
      "id": "Q01",
      "primary": "incorrect",
      "effective": "incorrect",
      "reason": "All requested facts are present, but the prose supplies a materially contrary Fear-deck preparation instruction. The stage counts and Invader quotation make the likely intended word apparent; nevertheless this question expressly asks how both decks are prepared, and the written instruction assigns a distinct shuffle/removal procedure to Fear. Correct quotations do not withdraw that operative instruction."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-a",
      "id": "Q20",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "partial",
      "reason": "The sacrifice case, timing, three earlier Terror conditions and defeat routes are complete. The fourth victory condition is incomplete: \u201cwin regardless of Invaders\u201d does not identify how that condition is reached, and its final-card earning/no-resolution details are absent throughout this entry."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-a",
      "id": "Q52",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "partial",
      "reason": "The Damage/Health answer is correct. The asked removal choice is expressly left unresolved, and no same-entry quotation supplies an unrestricted Remove ruling that resolves that caveat. The general summary definition can support the correct rule, but cannot be attributed to this reader as an answer it declined to give."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-a",
      "id": "Q85",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "partial",
      "reason": "The Fear, counterattack, Remove/Replace and Blight contrasts are complete, including Presence destruction in the attached quotation. The specific named-actor ruling remains expressly unresolved; a general correct quotation does not cancel that caveat."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-a",
      "id": "Q101",
      "primary": "incorrect",
      "effective": "correct",
      "reason": "The complete entry unambiguously retains Defend in the posed Ravage. \u201cYes\u201d is an isolated polarity slip, immediately resolved by the explicit answer sentence and reinforced by every substantive same-entry field; it supplies no competing operative ruling about lost Defend. No substantive contradiction or missing asked fact remains."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q02",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "partial",
      "reason": "The Presence-placement and Energy rules are correct, but the question separately asks how uncovered Card Plays numbers combine. That rule appears nowhere in this reader\u2019s complete Q02 entry."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q37",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "correct",
      "reason": "All asked parts are resolved. The negative automatic-play answer, reinforced by the quotation placing the gained card in hand, also unambiguously excludes automatic resolution of that unplayed newly gained card. This credits ordinary equivalent meaning, not a calculation or invented missing case result."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q50",
      "primary": "partial",
      "effective": "partial",
      "reason": "The sentence about this turn\u2019s already completed Build is chronologically true and does not assert that the new Explorer itself Built. It leaves the literal future-Build question unanswered, including the next-turn queue and prevention by removing the last Invader. Partial rather than a material wrong-rule finding is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "reader": "reader-b",
      "id": "Q52",
